  "findings": [
    "Errors show a strong tendency to output 10K across different true values; this is an observed output pattern, not proof of its cause.",
    "Downsampling from 2400 to 1024 pixels makes many labels tiny. Some target labels remain readable to this reviewer, and one original render has overlapping labels.",
    "One failed validation answer gives 10K for a literal 10K Pack label: nominal resistance matches, but the printed qualification is omitted. Keep this distinct from numeric-value errors.",
    "Training labels are imbalanced; exact 10K appears in 72/172 image-only value labels, with more equivalent or qualified variants. Naive duplication of all vision rows preserves that imbalance."
  ],
  "recommended_order": [
    "Run the same frozen adapter on validation only at 1536 and/or 2048 pixels with matched decoding/history. Record context and completion failures; do not call a failed high-resolution run an accuracy improvement.",
    "Compare each validation value result against 1024 to distinguish resolution-sensitive errors from persistent target-association or label-prior errors.",
    "If needed, develop a training-only variant that gives image-only supervision more weight and balances value/part-label diversity. Preserve family split isolation; never add validation or heldout answers to training.",
    "Keep label-overlap ambiguity as an explicit render/input quality issue; investigate using validation/training originals before any separately versioned corpus repair. Do not silently edit the frozen benchmark."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Legibility assessment is qualitative and by this independent reviewer, not a measured OCR threshold.",
    "Full validation set contains only 26 value questions, and multi-turn gold history can provide correlated values for later questions.",
    "Resolution, training weighting, and label balancing are proposed hypotheses. No improvement is claimed until measured on validation."
  ]
}
